<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:44:37 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Europe</category><title>Kyiv power plant hit by Russian missile without warning from allies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-kyiv-power-plant-hit-by-russian-missile-without-warning-from-allies</link><description>
Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky said Tuesday that a Russian ballistic missile struck a Kyiv power plant without advance warning from Western allies, killing at least two people and wounding around 20. The attack came days after US President Donald Trump announced an energy ceasefire between Moscow and Kyiv, raising questions over efforts to halt strikes on critical infrastructure.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6b4a660-c75e-11f1-98ab-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286839487353.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6b4a660-c75e-11f1-98ab-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286839487353.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fae67824-c767-11f1-bb13-c5a9b4bd2820</guid><pubDate>Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:41:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6b4a660-c75e-11f1-98ab-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286839487353.jpg">© Evgeniy Maloletka, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pope Leo has cancerous growth removed in lung operation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-has-cancerous-growth-removed-in-lung-operation</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV had a cancerous growth removed from his right lung in a 90-minute operation on Tuesday and "woke up normally" after the procedure, the Vatican said. A Vatican source said further tests were being carried out to determine if the cancer had spread. "To ensure the procedure was radical, the lower lobe of the right lung was removed," the Vatican said in a statement. FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta reports from Rome.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16231fa6-c74b-11f1-a4f0-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-230330-230812-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/16231fa6-c74b-11f1-a4f0-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-230330-230812-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1b51ea8e-c74b-11f1-aa5e-db1448cc4d3c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:23:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ceuta an 'inalienable' part of Spain, king says on key visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ceuta-an-inalienable-part-of-spain-king-says-on-key-visit</link><description>
King Felipe VI on Tuesday said Ceuta and Melilla were "an inalienable part" of Spain as he made a landmark visit to the north African territories claimed by neighbouring Morocco. "Ceuta and Melilla are an inalienable part of the political and national reality that is Spain. The sovereignty and territorial integrity of our country are not negotiable," Felipe said. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd4d9a70-c737-11f1-948a-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-203549-204111-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd4d9a70-c737-11f1-948a-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-203549-204111-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e3170b12-c737-11f1-aa53-d798fadc02e5</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:06:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>King Felipe VI says Ceuta is ‘inalienable’ part of Spain in landmark visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-spanish-royals-visit-ceuta-amid-tensions-with-morocco-over-migrant-influx</link><description>
King Felipe VI and Queen Letizia visited Ceuta on Tuesday for the first time in 14 years, with the monarch reaffirming Spain’s sovereignty over the North African enclaves claimed by Morocco. The landmark visit comes amid strained relations with Rabat and the aftermath of a mass migrant influx that saw makeshift camps cleared ahead of the royals’ arrival.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a609bdbc-c711-11f1-9672-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286426125316.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a609bdbc-c711-11f1-9672-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286426125316.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ed7deb02-c714-11f1-8a12-33956213bea6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:17:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a609bdbc-c711-11f1-9672-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286426125316.jpg">© Manu Fernandez, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Belgium: Greener schools thanks to European funding</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/belgium-greener-schools-thanks-to-european-funding</link><description>
🇧🇪 In Ganshoren, in Belgium, a new school replaces run-down buildings. But the need for renovations remains enormous.👉🏻 Find the whole reporting on France 24 English. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1a4cd9a-c70e-11f1-a119-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/Greener-schools.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b1a4cd9a-c70e-11f1-a119-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/Greener-schools.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">95428516-c70e-11f1-80b7-914b699b402e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:27:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia pounds Ukrainian cities, spares energy targets for first time since Trump 'ceasefire'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-russia-pounds-ukrainian-cities-spares-energy-targets-for-first-time-since-trump-ceasefire</link><description>
Russia hammered Ukrainian cities and transport links overnight into Tuesday, killing at least four people in the city of Kharkiv, while appearing to spare energy facilities for the first time since US President Donald Trump announced an "energy ceasefire" at the weekend. It was not clear whether Moscow had deliberately avoided targeting power plants.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c325c39e-c704-11f1-8f59-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-13T090934Z-1644364573-RC282OAZNFIH-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KHARKIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c325c39e-c704-11f1-8f59-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-13T090934Z-1644364573-RC282OAZNFIH-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KHARKIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8171a586-c703-11f1-9a3d-3b1e1fb2f193</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:39:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c325c39e-c704-11f1-8f59-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-13T090934Z-1644364573-RC282OAZNFIH-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KHARKIV.jpg">© Sofiia Gatilova, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spanish royals visit crisis-hit Ceuta amid diplomatic tensions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/spanish-royals-visit-crisis-hit-ceuta-amid-diplomatic-tensions</link><description>
Spain’s King Felipe VI and Queen Letizia visited Ceuta for the first time since 2007, amid tensions with Morocco following July’s migration crisis, when more than 70,000 people crossed into the Spanish enclave. Most returned to Morocco, but thousands remained, and dozens died. Morocco claims sovereignty over Ceuta, making the royal visit diplomatically sensitive. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris has more from Madrid.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e6c8475a-c663-11f1-a7a4-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-12T095944Z-1631494925-RC2L1OAGSDDU-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-NATIONAL-DAY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e6c8475a-c663-11f1-a7a4-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-12T095944Z-1631494925-RC2L1OAGSDDU-RTRMADP-3-SPAIN-NATIONAL-DAY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">97223c96-c704-11f1-ad22-ff6afdbff2d2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:30:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>'Transactional diplomacy': Greece positioning itself as Trump's most 'reliable ally in the region'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261013-transactional-diplomacy-greece-positioning-itself-as-the-us-most-reliable-ally-in-the-region</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Petros Konstantinidis, a financial journalist for Greece's leading daily newspaper TA NEA. The current controversy surrounding the US ambassador to Greece, Kimberly Guilfoyle, has all the makings of a reality TV show or a telenovela, or both. "This is diplomacy under Trump turning into lifestyle diplomacy," Konstantinidis explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/832a9522-c71c-11f1-b142-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-41d692d4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/832a9522-c71c-11f1-b142-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-41d692d4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">147ed8ca-c6fb-11f1-b2d6-55ed6e285468</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:41:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Spain’s king visits Ceuta amid tensions with Morocco</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/spain-s-king-visits-ceuta-amid-tensions-with-morocco</link><description>
King Felipe VI and Queen Letizia are visiting Ceuta months after more than 70,000 migrants arrived from Morocco. While most have returned, thousands remain. The visit has divided residents and risks reigniting diplomatic tensions with Morocco, which claims sovereignty over Ceuta and Melilla.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bdf9123c-9ca6-11f1-bc45-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-20T124328Z-1284655205-RC292NADIEOA-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bdf9123c-9ca6-11f1-bc45-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-20T124328Z-1284655205-RC292NADIEOA-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5e496190-c6e3-11f1-a6a4-a57396bb95c6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:22:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Pope Leo XIV admitted to hospital for lung surgery</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/pope-leo-xiv-admitted-to-hospital-for-lung-surgery</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV has been admitted to Rome’s Gemelli hospital for surgery to remove a small lung nodule discovered during recent medical checks. The 71-year-old pontiff said the growth was detected at an early stage. The procedure marks his first hospitalisation since becoming pope in May 2025. FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta has the latest from Rome.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2c428f50-bb58-11f1-a1b9-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-28T155925Z-496606537-RC2FSNABCLSJ-RTRMADP-3-POPE-FRANCE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2c428f50-bb58-11f1-a1b9-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-28T155925Z-496606537-RC2FSNABCLSJ-RTRMADP-3-POPE-FRANCE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3e85d8ec-c6e4-11f1-943e-d1eabdeaa934</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:20:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>French students ‘not giving up the fight’ as 480,000 join new day of school protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-live-france-braces-for-fresh-nationwide-protests-over-school-conditions</link><description>
French students staged another day of nationwide protests on Tuesday over poor school conditions, including teacher shortages and dilapidated buildings, vowing to keep up the pressure ahead of half-term holidays. Around 480,000 protesters joined in on the demonstrations, with Swedish activist Greta Thunberg turning up in Paris to boost the movement’s visibility. Read our liveblog to see how all the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd6f4a26-c6fc-11f1-a88b-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D33T8FC.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd6f4a26-c6fc-11f1-a88b-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D33T8FC.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1c993a20-c6b8-11f1-90f5-25e5951a136a</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 06:44:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cd6f4a26-c6fc-11f1-a88b-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D33T8FC.jpg">© Sébastien Salom-Gomis, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>'A positive step': Hungary removes anti-LGBTQ provisions from Orban-era law</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-a-positive-step-hungary-removes-anti-lgbtq-provisions-from-orban-era-law</link><description>
Hungary's parliament voted on Tuesday to remove anti-LGBTQ provisions from a "child protection" law adopted in 2021 under the country's former nationalist leader, in the first significant move to reverse discriminatory legislation since Prime Minister Peter Magyar took power in May.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/223ee882-c6c5-11f1-ace6-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/6bbf472190d7c9d073a23b8d17644fa7b2c97d79.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/223ee882-c6c5-11f1-ace6-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/6bbf472190d7c9d073a23b8d17644fa7b2c97d79.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">22f5d394-c6c5-11f1-8cbf-7d59f89cb4d8</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:15:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/223ee882-c6c5-11f1-ace6-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/6bbf472190d7c9d073a23b8d17644fa7b2c97d79.jpg">© Attila Kisbenedek, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia says Europe bought $320 billion in hydrocarbons since 2022</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261013-russia-says-europe-bought-320-billion-in-hydrocarbons-since-2022</link><description>
Russia said on Monday that European Union countries had bought $320.7 billion worth of its energy resources since 2022, despite sanctions over the war in Ukraine. The figure fuelled tensions as European officials criticised a US deal to import Russian diesel, while Stockholm called for the bloc to use frozen Russian assets to boost support for Kyiv.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af462b9c-c6a6-11f1-aa6d-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/1a5bd83c4347c7ff92f5c51031b917a553b7d6de.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af462b9c-c6a6-11f1-aa6d-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/1a5bd83c4347c7ff92f5c51031b917a553b7d6de.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9b6d6754-c6b3-11f1-9184-cfb9f08dc45e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:10:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af462b9c-c6a6-11f1-aa6d-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/1a5bd83c4347c7ff92f5c51031b917a553b7d6de.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Pope Leo diagnosed with lung cancer after doctors successfully remove nodule</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-what-we-know-about-pope-leo-xiv-planned-lung-operation-this-week</link><description>
Pope ​Leo had a lower lobe ​of his right lung removed during surgery on Tuesday ​and ‌was diagnosed with lung ⁠adenocarcinoma, a common form of ‌lung cancer, the Vatican said in ⁠a medical bulletin. The surgery was successful and the pope is expected to spend a week in hospital recovering. The 71-year-old pontiff is due to travel to Uruguay, Argentina and Peru on November 6, though the Vatican has not confirmed the operation date.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ffe29c06-c742-11f1-9581-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D34D2T4-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ffe29c06-c742-11f1-9581-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D34D2T4-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">341b2af0-c68b-11f1-be6c-c1e164f0c3a6</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 22:20:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ffe29c06-c742-11f1-9581-e362370cce2e/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D34D2T4-1.jpg">© Handout photo, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>'It's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington,' analyst says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261012-it-s-clear-that-moscow-is-just-playing-with-washington-analyst-says</link><description>
US President Donald Trump's envoys told ​Ukrainian officials on Friday that a deal to allow Russian diesel exports is part of a bid to draw Russia back to negotiations after the failure of previous efforts to launch sustained talks to end the war, three people familiar with the meeting told Reuters. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Grégoire Roos, director of the Europe and Russia and Eurasia Programmes at Chatham House. He says that "it's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington because Vladimir Putin knows that Donald Trump lives on borrowed time".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9f7551c-c6f6-11f1-8056-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5989657066ace121c0028d9-88156669.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9f7551c-c6f6-11f1-8056-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5989657066ace121c0028d9-88156669.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2e1ca0d0-c680-11f1-a597-39b90e59a506</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:02:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'It's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington,' analyst says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/it-s-clear-that-moscow-is-just-playing-with-washington-analyst-says</link><description>
US President Donald Trump's envoys told ​Ukrainian officials on Friday that a deal to allow Russian diesel exports is part of a bid to draw Russia back to negotiations after the failure of previous efforts to launch sustained talks to end the war, three people familiar with the meeting told Reuters. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Grégoire Roos, director of the Europe and Russia and Eurasia Programmes at Chatham House. He says that "it's clear that Moscow is just playing with Washington because Vladimir Putin knows that Donald Trump lives on borrowed time".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9f7551c-c6f6-11f1-8056-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5989657066ace121c0028d9-88156669.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f9f7551c-c6f6-11f1-8056-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5989657066ace121c0028d9-88156669.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f291f4e4-c67e-11f1-98b9-0f55d11f6695</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:58:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Tehran denies involvement in UK Fairford air base incident as Britain summons Iranian ambassador</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-tehran-denies-involvement-in-uk-fairford-air-base-incident-as-britain-summons-iranian-ambassador</link><description>
British Prime Minister Andy Burnham on Monday accused Iran's Revolutionary Guards of being responsible for a terror-related incident in September at England's Fairford air base, which is used by the United States military. Following Tehran's denial, the British Foreign Office summoned Iran's Ambassador for talks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f62725c0-c674-11f1-b28d-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T121509Z-308014431-RC2ZSNAMCV4D-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f62725c0-c674-11f1-b28d-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T121509Z-308014431-RC2ZSNAMCV4D-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0977e710-c673-11f1-80cc-f3f08e592561</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:23:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f62725c0-c674-11f1-b28d-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-29T121509Z-308014431-RC2ZSNAMCV4D-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-USA-FAIRFORD.jpg">© Toby Shepheard, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Increasingly evident' Russia won't accept 'energy ceasefire': Zelensky</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/increasingly-evident-russia-won-t-accept-energy-ceasefire-zelensky</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said Monday it was clear that Russia would not agree to stop hitting energy targets, after US President Donald Trump unilaterally announced a deal between the warring nations. "It is increasingly evident that Russia is unwilling to accept an energy ceasefire proposed by the United States," Zelensky said on social media. FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de7a2f66-0d70-11f1-b26c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-01-28T160607Z-351041766-RC2U7JAOLLPY-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ENERGY-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de7a2f66-0d70-11f1-b26c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-01-28T160607Z-351041766-RC2U7JAOLLPY-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ENERGY-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fd90ac34-c672-11f1-aaa6-cb91b9ab5e34</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:40:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'A lot of Ukrainians are feeling extremely betrayed' by Trump's Russian diesel deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/a-lot-of-ukrainians-are-feeling-extremely-betrayed-by-trump-s-russian-diesel-deal</link><description>
Reporting from central Ukraine, FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg says that "a lot of Ukrainians are feeling extremely betrayed by a country that until recently they saw not only as an ally but as a beacon of freedom and democracy, a country whose values they should aspire to. All of that is falling apart very quickly and Ukrainians' admiration for the United States is disintegrating."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eed7c2c6-c66e-11f1-80dc-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-200509-200949-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eed7c2c6-c66e-11f1-80dc-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-200509-200949-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f3fd3312-c66e-11f1-832b-f5ddaf84e408</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:04:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>How has the European Union’s major recovery plan benefited the 27 member states?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-how-has-the-more-than-%E2%82%AC600-billion-recovery-plan-revitalised-europe</link><description>
The 27 member states of the European Union agreed in July 2020 on a €750 billion post-Covid recovery plan called NextGenerationEU. Its main instrument is the Recovery and Resilience Facility, through which the European Commission has already disbursed €450 billion out of €573 billion. The programme is due to come to an end in a few months. The Commission is currently assessing Member States’ claims for the remaining funds.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a368a8d0-c625-11f1-a0b7-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-PKG-ALIX-SALLE-DE-CLASSE.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a368a8d0-c625-11f1-a0b7-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-PKG-ALIX-SALLE-DE-CLASSE.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">efd12616-c634-11f1-8f6e-b3d04d2883e3</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:19:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a368a8d0-c625-11f1-a0b7-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/PHOTO-PKG-ALIX-SALLE-DE-CLASSE.png">© FRANCE 24</source><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>EU warns online platforms over livestreaming US execution planned by Pentagon</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-eu-warns-online-platforms-over-livestreaming-us-execution-planned-by-pentagon</link><description>
The European Union warned digital platforms on Monday against livestreaming the execution of Nidal Hasan, a former US Army psychiatrist who is scheduled to be executed by firing squad on December 3 for killing 13 people at a military base in 2009. Under EU rules, platforms have an obligation to moderate shocking and violent content, including capital punishment.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/85cd6d82-c644-11f1-b8ef-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2NZ3T3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/85cd6d82-c644-11f1-b8ef-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2NZ3T3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6c522638-c642-11f1-ab3a-5f09709176c3</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:05:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/85cd6d82-c644-11f1-b8ef-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D2NZ3T3.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>NATO's top US commander warns Russia that any 'foolish' attack on allies would be 'futile'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-nato-s-top-us-commander-warns-russia-that-any-foolish-attack-on-allies-would-be-futile</link><description>
NATO's top US military commander in Europe said Monday that any "foolish" attack on the alliance would be "utterly futile", a warning to Russia as European fears grow over the threat from Moscow that includes "hybrid" warfare and cyberattacks. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f3aadfbe-c5dc-11f1-a00a-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/37a7a837cd1d509e11c2654af36581affca3d9ea.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f3aadfbe-c5dc-11f1-a00a-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/37a7a837cd1d509e11c2654af36581affca3d9ea.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">46b25518-c63a-11f1-a40f-2dd75a13a6e7</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:41:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f3aadfbe-c5dc-11f1-a00a-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/37a7a837cd1d509e11c2654af36581affca3d9ea.jpg">© Nicolas Maetermink, Belga / AFP </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: NATO's top military commander warns Russia over alleged sabotage</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/replay-nato-s-top-military-commander-warns-russia-over-alleged-sabotage</link><description>
And as the war in Ukraine continues, Western concerns are growing over Moscow’s alleged campaign of sabotage and interference against Kiev's wartime backers. NATO's top military commander gave a press conference this Monday from Warsaw. US General Alexus Grynkewich looks set to warn Russia over the alliance’s ability to counter-attack. Analysis by FRANCE 24 International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f93dadda-c636-11f1-abe7-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-131234-133046-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f93dadda-c636-11f1-abe7-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-131234-133046-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fe8bc60a-c636-11f1-b4ca-75ff764c78f1</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:26:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine: Zelensky says learned of Trump's 'energy ceasefire' through media</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-zelensky-says-learned-of-trump-s-energy-ceasefire-through-media</link><description>
An Axios report is citing an unnamed US source who says that Donald Trump's surprise energy ceasefire between Russia and Ukraine only concerns oil refineries. Elitsa Gadeva explains what this would mean for both sides.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0dc19ab6-c630-11f1-b68c-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-120216-120402-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0dc19ab6-c630-11f1-b68c-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-120216-120402-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">12fd2522-c630-11f1-a33c-2bb1d710b13a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:24:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Prison 'Games of Hope' olympics in Italy unite inmates and staff</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/prison-games-of-hope-olympics-in-italy-unite-inmates-and-staff</link><description>
Sport has the power to unite, and overcome barriers... In Rome, inmates and prison officers became athletes for the day, and took part in a sort of mini prison olympics. Organised by the John Paul II foundation for sport, this is the third edition of the “Games of Hope”, over a year after it was held in the men's wing of the prison in 2025. Story by Emily Boyle.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe1e4916-c629-11f1-b215-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-091213-091346-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe1e4916-c629-11f1-b215-77317c09f325/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-091213-091346-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0308d720-c62a-11f1-9855-31f546c55914</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:54:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Poland: Police foils alleged assassination attempt against PM</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/poland-police-foils-alleged-assassination-attempt-against-pm</link><description>
Poland's interior ministry said Sunday a man had been detained on suspicion of plotting an attack against Prime Minister Donald Tusk and Defence minister Wladyslaw Kosiniak-Kamysz. Interior minister Marcin Kierwinski told Polish media that the suspect, a man in his 60s, had been arrested in the southwestern region of Lower Silesia. He was identified through an analysis of content posted online. The man's home is being searched and his contacts examined. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Warsaw, Adrien Sarlat.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e7d13e6-c62a-11f1-9df1-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-100343-100644-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e7d13e6-c62a-11f1-9df1-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-100343-100644-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">636f9d9c-c62a-11f1-a4cf-1b9a714fd227</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:52:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Are European automakers capable of withstanding Chinese competition?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/are-european-automakers-capable-of-withstanding-chinese-competition</link><description>
The Paris Motor Show opens its doors today, and with it come mounting economic and diplomatic issues. The European Union has just announced that it has secured a commitment from China to moderate the flow of hybrid vehicles into the block's market. It opens the prospect of cutting China's export by more than a half and could prevent millions of Chinese cars from being shipped to Europe. Are European automakers capable of withstanding this competition and their dependence on China? This report from France 2 and Morgan Ayre.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b23c0e66-c624-11f1-b7ee-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-084242-084440-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b23c0e66-c624-11f1-b7ee-29a2e29ae696/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261012-084242-084440-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b748f7f2-c624-11f1-b11a-019eccf14e4d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:26:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Zelensky says surprised to hear about Trump's 'energy ceasefire' between Ukraine and Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/zelensky-says-surprised-to-hear-about-trump-s-energy-ceasefire-between-ukraine-and-russia</link><description>
Ukrainian power plants were hit by Russian strikes on Sunday, leading to power outages. President Volodymyr Zelensky announced the attacks and expressed his surprise at the US President's post that stated that an “energy ceasefire” had been agreed upon between Ukraine and Russia. While Zelensky said he was not aware of any deal he said he would welcome one. Moscow has yet to confirm any accord. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Kyiv, Gulliver Cragg.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1f72c30-c55b-11f1-941b-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-09T204400Z-1727445418-RC2WZNAE754C-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-USA-DIESEL-UKRAINE-ZELENSKIY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f1f72c30-c55b-11f1-941b-53993c5f1f18/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-09T204400Z-1727445418-RC2WZNAE754C-RTRMADP-3-RUSSIA-USA-DIESEL-UKRAINE-ZELENSKIY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">704c058e-c623-11f1-ac63-8b5dc0aa6046</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:19:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Americans Robert E. Hall and Michael Woodford win Nobel Prize in Economics</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261012-americans-robert-e-hall-and-michael-woodford-win-nobel-prize-in-economics</link><description>
The 2026 Nobel economics prize has been awarded to US economists ⁠Robert Hall ​and Michael Woodford, the Royal Swedish Academy of ‌Sciences said on Monday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2f7c8b6-c622-11f1-bac3-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/Nobel-Eco.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2f7c8b6-c622-11f1-bac3-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/Nobel-Eco.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0bbb0170-c61d-11f1-b601-83431ceca236</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 09:54:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2f7c8b6-c622-11f1-bac3-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/Nobel-Eco.jpg">© Nobel Prize Outreach</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump touts surprise 'energy ceasefire' – Zelensky says he hasn't seen details, Moscow silent</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261012-trump-touts-surprise-energy-ceasefire-%E2%80%93-zelensky-says-he-hasn-t-seen-details-moscow-silent</link><description>
The US President Donald Trump sowed confusion on Sunday, announcing an "energy ceasefire" between Ukraine and Russia. Kyiv expressed astonishment, there was silence from Moscow. Ukrainian strikes have wreaked havoc on the Russian oil industry. Were there to be an "energy ceasefire" it could allow Moscow to repair refineries. For Ukraine, it could safeguard vital energy infrastructure. Story by Nicholas Rushworth.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db49974e-c61d-11f1-b573-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T004527Z-1640129275-RC2O0OA8PKYS-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db49974e-c61d-11f1-b573-3774aeac812a/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-11T004527Z-1640129275-RC2O0OA8PKYS-RTRMADP-3-USA-TRUMP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3baeba8e-c61d-11f1-9666-2f42f8430027</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 09:19:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
